    "final_text": "I fixed ISSUE-214. `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`, and all 10 tests pass (7 existing plus 3 new).\n\n**Root cause:** in `src/url-builder.js`, `serializeQuery` skipped query values with `if (!value)`. That check treats `0` and `false` the same as a missing value, so they were dropped. `appendQueryValue` had the same check for array items, so `attempt: [0, 1]` also lost its `0`.\n\n**Fix:** a 9-line change in `src/url-builder.js`. Both checks now call a small `isOmittedQueryValue` helper, which skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`. The public API is unchanged.\n\n**One decision to review:** I kept empty strings dropped, as before. Common libraries like `qs` would write `cursor=` instead, but switching would affect any existing caller that relies on empty fields disappearing, and the issue only covers `0` and `false`. Say if you want to change that separately.\n\n**Tests** (in `tests/url-builder.test.js`):\n- `buildUrl keeps retry=0 and include_archived=false query values (ISSUE-214)` uses the exact case from the issue.\n- `serializeQuery keeps 0 and false items inside array values` covers the array path.\n- `serializeQuery still skips null, undefined, and empty-string values` checks that values skipped before are still skipped.\n\nI ran the first two against the unfixed code and both failed with the reported symptom (the URL was `...?dry_run=true` only). The third passes either way.\n\n**Verification:** the full suite passed through `dx run-gate --name full-gate`. The project has no linter configured, so none was run. Nothing is left running.\n\n`ISSUE.md` now ends with a `Resolution` section naming the code path, the fix and the three tests. I haven't committed anything; the changes are uncommitted in the working tree on `main`.",
